"""
woam - machine memory for redu.cloud.

WHAT THIS IS
    A record of what changed on this machine and why, partitioned into functional
    groups, so the next agent (or you, at 2am) does not rediscover it.

THE ONE RULE
    If you changed something in a group, record it. One command, a few tokens.
    That is cheap against the thousands of tokens the next agent burns working it
    out again, or worse, working from a wrong assumption.

WHY IT IS BUILT THIS WAY
    - Reading is a private good: the reader benefits, so it only has to be useful.
    - Writing is a public good: the writer pays, someone else benefits. So it is
      required, not requested. `woam status` fails while a group is unrecorded.
    - Volatile facts are stored as a QUERY to run, never as an answer, so they
      cannot go stale. A stale answer is worse than none: without it you check,
      with it you trust.
    - The log is append-only JSONL. One line per record, under PIPE_BUF, so
      concurrent appends are atomic and a torn write costs one record, not the file.
    - If you read something here that is WRONG, fixing it is your job: `woam fix`.
      Nothing here is guaranteed correct. It is guaranteed honest about provenance.

No dependencies beyond the Python 3 standard library. Runs on a redu VM, on a
plain Ubuntu box, or on a laptop.
"""

